---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const projects = [
  {
    id: 'ni',
    title: 'Notational Intelligence as Commit Law',
    deck: 'System One decides in software. WCA decides whether the machine is allowed to move.',
    status: 'Research study · draft',
    about: '/about/ni',
    paper: '/papers/ni/',
    pdf: '/pdfs/ni.pdf',
    figures: '/living/ni/',
    tags: ['commit law', 'MCP gate', 'analytical energy'],
  },
  {
    id: 'satiation',
    title: 'Satiation & Scarcity after Free AI',
    deck: 'Capability scales. Appetite does not. Design to done.',
    status: 'Research study · draft',
    about: '/about/satiation',
    paper: '/papers/satiation/',
    pdf: '/pdfs/satiation.pdf',
    figures: '/living/satiation/',
    tags: ['satiation', 'scarcity', 'bliss surface'],
  },
  {
    id: 'mol',
    title: 'Mixture of Limits — Navigation Law for Computer Intelligence',
    deck: 'Floors where more bits stop buying outcomes. Compression and formulas beat excess tokens; NN is a demoted residual leaf.',
    status: 'Research study · draft',
    about: '/about/mol',
    paper: '/papers/mol/',
    pdf: '/pdfs/mol.pdf',
    figures: '/living/mol/',
    tags: ['mixture of limits', 'VoI floors', 'Landauer estimate'],
  },
  {
    id: 'mei',
    title: 'Metabolic Intelligence: Budget-Native Compute from Tag to Campus',
    deck: 'A budget goes in; the best answer that budget can buy comes out. Digital enzymes at microwatts; grid-following service at 100 MW.',
    status: 'Research study · draft',
    about: '/about/mei',
    paper: '/papers/mei/',
    pdf: '/pdfs/mei.pdf',
    figures: '/living/mei/',
    tags: ['metabolic intelligence', 'budget-native', 'OpenADR', 'digital enzymes'],
  },
];
---

<Layout title="Research catalog" description="OpenIE research studies: readable papers, downloadable PDFs, and interactive figures. Stage C programmed Alchitry Pt V2 (energy Unmetered there). KV260 INA260 Metered for WCA seed watts/pJ/op.">
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">research.openie.dev</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-white max-w-3xl">
      Research catalog
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base md:text-lg text-brand-slate max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      Readable research studies with downloadable PDFs. Interactive figures under <span class="text-brand-cyan">/living/</span> are companions - not the papers themselves.
      Research studies. Analytical energy is not board power. Stage C programmed an Alchitry Pt V2; energy remains unmetered on that board. KV260 INA260 Metered for WCA seed and richer LUT∧PH∧CBF gate (watts + pJ/op) (see /living/fpga-sim/alchitry/#energy). Pt V2 remains Unmetered.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/ni/" class="inline-flex items-center font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read NI paper
      </a>
      <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="inline-flex items-center font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors">
        Read Satiation paper
      </a>
      <a href="/papers/mol/" class="inline-flex items-center font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Read Mixture of Limits paper
      </a>
      <a href="/papers/mei/" class="inline-flex items-center font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Read Metabolic Intelligence paper
      </a>
      <a href="/living/" class="inline-flex items-center font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        Figures hub
      </a>
      <a href="/living/fpga-sim/alchitry/" class="inline-flex items-center font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Alchitry guide
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="companion-laws" class="px-6 md:px-10 pb-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="glass-card p-6 md:p-8">
      <p class="section-label mb-3">Catalog triad</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-brand-white mb-3">Navigation / Commit / Economic Reality of Satiation</h2>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-5">
        Three studies compose one stack. Mixture of Limits navigates. Notational Intelligence owns irreversible commit. Satiation owns Economic Reality of Satiation. They do not collapse into one paper. Analytical estimates are not board power; package <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code> only when Metered.
      </p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <a href="/papers/mol/" class="block rounded-lg border border-brand-border p-4 no-underline hover:border-brand-cyan/50 transition-colors">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-cyan mb-2">Navigation</p>
          <p class="text-brand-white text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Mixture of Limits</p>
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Lookup → Formula → Solver → Model LAST. Floors: Value of Information (VoI), grammar, energy estimate, certificate, settle-refuse.</p>
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] text-brand-gray mt-3">/papers/mol/</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/papers/ni/" class="block rounded-lg border border-brand-border p-4 no-underline hover:border-brand-amber/50 transition-colors">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-amber mb-2">Commit</p>
          <p class="text-brand-white text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Notational Intelligence as Commit Law</p>
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">propose → certify → commit|refuse → receipt. Notational Intelligence owns the irreversible commit record.</p>
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] text-brand-gray mt-3">/papers/ni/</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="block rounded-lg border border-brand-border p-4 no-underline hover:border-brand-gold/50 transition-colors">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gold mb-2">Economic Reality of Satiation</p>
          <p class="text-brand-white text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Satiation and Scarcity after Free AI</p>
          <p class="font-body text-xs text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Stop when VoI is zero on a stated completeness predicate, or when budget / policy refuse fires.</p>
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] text-brand-gray mt-3">/papers/satiation/</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <pre class="mt-5 font-mono text-[10px] md:text-[11px] text-brand-slate leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto bg-black/20 border border-brand-border rounded-lg p-4">┌─ Navigation — Mixture of Limits ─────────────────────────┐
│  Lookup → Formula → Solver → Model LAST                  │
└────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                             ▼
┌─ Commit — Notational Intelligence as Commit Law ─────────┐
│  propose → certify → commit|refuse → receipt             │
└────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                             ▼
┌─ Economic Reality of Satiation — Satiation and Scarcity after Free AI ───┐
│  VoI = 0 on C(z), or budget / policy hit                 │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section id="metabolic-intelligence" class="px-6 md:px-10 pb-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="glass-card p-6 md:p-8">
      <p class="section-label mb-3">Fourth study · energy budget</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-brand-white mb-3">Metabolic Intelligence</h2>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-5">
        The catalog triad (Navigation / Commit / Economic Reality of Satiation) stays intact.
        Metabolic Intelligence is a fourth study: energy-budget embodiment from microwatt tags to a 100 MW grid-following campus.
        A budget goes in; the best answer that budget can buy comes out. Soft-ref path:
        <code class="text-brand-cyan">board_synth_claimed=false</code>; estimates ≠ package <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code>.
      </p>
      <a href="/papers/mei/" class="block rounded-lg border border-brand-border p-4 no-underline hover:border-brand-cyan/50 transition-colors max-w-xl">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-cyan mb-2">Energy budget / metabolic embodiment</p>
        <p class="text-brand-white text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Metabolic Intelligence</p>
        <p class="font-body text-xs text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Digital enzymes + J(m|q) obtain-router + OpenADR/MQTT service. Physics-informed, test-time, sequential learning; no large pretrain on the enzyme path. Dual-map: GPU/MCU today; neuromorphic / analog / photonic / adiabatic next.</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] text-brand-gray mt-3">/papers/mei/</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="catalog" class="px-6 md:px-10 pb-20 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="flex items-end justify-between gap-4 mb-8">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label mb-2">Catalog</p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-white">Research studies</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-brand-gray hidden sm:block">board_synth_claimed=false</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      {projects.map((p) => (
        <article class="glass-card p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-amber">{p.status}</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-brand-gray">{p.id}</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-brand-white mb-3">{p.title}</h3>
          <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed flex-1">{p.deck}</p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-5 mb-6">
            {p.tags.map((t) => (
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] px-2 py-1 rounded border border-brand-border text-brand-gray">{t}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a href={p.paper} class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber no-underline hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">
              Read paper →
            </a>
            <a href={p.pdf} class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan no-underline hover:text-brand-teal transition-colors" download>
              Download PDF
            </a>
            <a href={p.figures} class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
              Figures
            </a>
            <a href={p.about} class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-gray no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
              About
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pb-24 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="glass-card p-6 md:p-8">
      <p class="section-label mb-3">Measurement</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl text-brand-white mb-3">Research studies, not journal finals</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
        <li>Prose lives at <code class="text-brand-cyan">/papers/</code>; real PDFs at <code class="text-brand-cyan">/pdfs/</code>.</li>
        <li>Interactive figures stay under <code class="text-brand-cyan">/living/</code> - companions, not paper shells sold as papers.</li>
        <li>No Notion AI, Elicit, Consensus, or other paid research services in the runtime.</li>
        <li>Claim ledgers bind web, PDF, Medium, demos, and metadata. Forbidden claims stay off the UI.</li>
        <li>Stage C programmed an Alchitry Pt V2 (SRAM; energy still unmetered on Pt V2). KV260 INA260 Metered for WCA seed and gate fabrics (watts + pJ/op). OpCounter joules elsewhere are analytical estimates, not board power. Guide: <a href="/living/fpga-sim/alchitry/#energy" class="text-brand-cyan no-underline hover:text-brand-teal">/living/fpga-sim/alchitry/#energy</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
